{"id":"000VX7","title":"Chaotic Internal Skyscrapers","author":"yttrio","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T23:14:41+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 22:44 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is part of the puzzle pack Chaotic Construction by the Sudoku Skunkworks. Please check it out!\n\nRules:\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into regions of 9 orthogonally connected cells each, such that every cell is part of exactly one region. Place the digits 1 to 9 exactly once in each row, column and region.\n\nOne internal region border is given.\n\nInternal skyscrapers: A cell in the direction of an arrow is visible, if its digit is larger than all digits in the cells located strictly between the arrow cell and itself. The digit in an arrow cell indicates the number of visible cells in the direction of the arrow. Additionally, every visible cell must be in the same region as the arrow cell and every not visible cell must be in a different region than the arrow cell.\n\nAn example grid (not intended to be solvable) is given below. For a solvable 6x6 puzzle with the rule set, you can find it in the pack :)\n\nSudokuPad - Penpa+","solutionCode":"Row 7, with \"-\" for region borders","tags":["Sudoku","Hochhäuser","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/pr2irr72p7","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/2bcp4d64","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/pr2irr72p7","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T23:14:41+00:00"}